The change log can be viewed at:

https://github.com/kiloscheffer/zunzun-ng/commits/master

The pre-fork (zunzunsite3) change log is preserved at the dormant
upstream repository:

https://bitbucket.org/zunzuncode/zunzunsite3/commits/all

--- Notable changes (summarised here; full history on GitHub) ---

chore/pyeq3-pr9-drop-bridges (merged 2026-06)
  Upstream equations-project/pyeq3 merged PR #9 (authored from pyeq3-ng),
  relaxing the numpy ceiling to >=1.24,<3 and declaring the pypandoc dep that
  pyeq3's package __init__ imports transitively. With both fixes upstream, the
  two local bridges from chore/pyeq3-upstream are now redundant: deleted the
  [tool.uv] override-dependencies that forced numpy 2.x AND the explicit pypandoc
  dependency. Bumped the [tool.uv.sources] pin from rev 3bfec02 (post-PR-#8) to
  ef97b62 (post-PR-#9) and re-locked. No fitting-code change — the only pyeq3
  source delta is a \cdot raw-string SyntaxWarning fix in Utilities.Multifit; the
  resolved environment (numpy 2.x, pypandoc) is unchanged. Upstream still has no
  release tag for this state, so the pin stays a rev=; switching to tag= remains
  a follow-up for when upstream cuts a release (see docs/operations/quarterly-
  upgrade.md watch list).

chore/pyeq3-upstream (merged 2026-06)
  Switched the pyeq3 dependency from the kiloscheffer/pyeq3-ng fork to upstream
  equations-project/pyeq3, pinned at the commit that merged the scipy.odr ->
  odrpack port (PR #8, authored from pyeq3-ng). Two stale-metadata gaps in
  upstream's pyproject are bridged locally until a fixed upstream tag exists:
  numpy is forced to 2.x via [tool.uv] override-dependencies (upstream still
  declares numpy<2.0), and pypandoc is declared as a direct dep (pyeq3's package
  __init__ eagerly imports Utilities.Multifit -> pypandoc, which upstream omits).
  No fitting-code change — the odr source is byte-identical between fork and
  upstream; the pyeq3-ng fork is now only a packaging delta, retireable once
  upstream relaxes numpy and declares pypandoc.

feat/demo-mode (merged 2026-06)
  New env-gated demo posture for public showcase deployments. ZUNZUN_DEMO_MODE=1
  caps fit-runs at DEMO_MAX_FITS_PER_HOUR (default 4, env override) per IP per
  hour — the run exceeding the ceiling gets a friendly HTTP 429 page instead of
  spawning a fit — and renders a faint diagonal "DEMO" watermark behind page
  content. Off by default; zero behavior change on a normal instance. The cap is
  an in-view guard (views.LongRunningProcessView) reusing the ratelimit cache;
  the watermark is pure CSS gated by a body class fed by a new context processor.

feat/debug-aware-concurrency-defaults (merged 2026-06)
  The concurrent-fit caps now default DEBUG-aware: under runserver (dev) both
  MAX_CONCURRENT_FITS_PER_SESSION and MAX_CONCURRENT_FITS_PER_IP relax to 10 so
  local multi-fit / FunctionFinder work isn't blocked by the one-at-a-time
  posture; under Waitress/WSGI (prod) they stay at the safe 1 and 4. Env vars
  (ZUNZUN_MAX_CONCURRENT_FITS_PER_SESSION / _PER_IP) still override either
  posture — the personal-production path. New settings._fits_default helper;
  prod behavior unchanged.

feat/ff-link-retention (merged 2026-06)
  Shared FunctionFinder links now live as long as a normal file-backed result
  (disk-bounded) instead of expiring at SESSION_COOKIE_AGE. A ranking completion
  drops an ffanchor_<pk> marker in temp/; _sweep_aged_rows no longer age-reaps
  ranking rows and _sweep_orphaned_terminal_rows reaps them when the size-prune
  removes the marker. FunctionFinderResults touches the marker on each render so
  active shares stay warm. Because a ranking's payload lives in LRPDispatchData
  (DB, uncounted toward the temp/ quota) and its marker is tiny, a hard age
  ceiling FF_RANKING_MAX_AGE (default 90d, env ZUNZUN_FF_RANKING_MAX_AGE_SECONDS)
  bounds row/DB growth for the case where the size-prune never fires. New
  _unique.py helpers ff_anchor_path / write_ff_anchor / touch_ff_anchor. Smoke
  asserts the marker appears after a ranking. Resolves BACKLOG "Shared
  FunctionFinder links expire at session-age".

chore/cross-dispatch-data-source (merged 2026-06)
  Cross-dispatch data reads promoted to a first-class typed concept. A new
  typed ChildPayload.data_source_pk field plus a _data_read_pk() resolver on
  StatusMonitoredLongRunningProcessPage: LoadItemFromSessionStore reads from
  data_source_pk when set, else status_row_pk (the write target). The
  FunctionFinderResults.LoadItemFromSessionStore override and the
  extra["ranking_status_pk"] bag key are deleted; the views.py interface-GET
  pre-fill no longer overloads status_row_pk for reads. No behavior change.

feat/functionfinder-token-binding (merged 2026-06)
  FunctionFinder ranking identity bound to result_token; concurrent-ranking
  collision fixed (#2785); FunctionFinder results now shareable cross-session
  (#2817) for ~2 weeks (until the ranking LRPStatus row ages out).

  Ranking identity now travels as &ranking=<result_token> in results URLs;
  _ranking_pk_from_token in zunzun/views.py resolves it. The single
  session["functionfinder_ranking_pk"] slot is fully retired. FunctionFinderResults
  sets cookie_test for token-bearing (cross-session) recipients so a cold
  session passes the pre-fit gate. Smoke: new function_finder_cross_session_2D
  scenario verifies a cookieless session can render the result.

feat/per-dispatch-isolation (merged 2026-06)
  Per-dispatch data isolation and concurrent-fits production posture.

  BREAKING CONFIG CHANGE: the `ALLOW_MULTIPLE_CONCURRENT_FITS_PER_USER`
  boolean is removed. Its True mode (unlimited concurrent fits per session)
  was the problematic default. Replace it with two explicit caps in
  settings.py:
    MAX_CONCURRENT_FITS_PER_SESSION  (default 1, matches old False mode)
    MAX_CONCURRENT_FITS_PER_IP       (default 4)
  Both are env-overridable:
    ZUNZUN_MAX_CONCURRENT_FITS_PER_SESSION
    ZUNZUN_MAX_CONCURRENT_FITS_PER_IP

  New model: LRPDispatchData (migration 0006_lrpdispatchdata_and_ownership)
    OneToOne -> LRPStatus, on_delete=CASCADE. Holds per-dispatch `data` and
    `functionfinder` JSON fields (encoder=NumpyJSONEncoder), replacing the
    old per-session SessionStore blobs keyed by session_key_data /
    session_key_functionfinder. Read/write via zunzun/dispatch_data.py.

  Shareable result links: every LRPStatus row auto-mints a unique
  result_token (secrets.token_urlsafe). On completion, the owner is
  redirected from /StatusAndResults/<pk>/ to /Results/<token>/. The token
  URL carries no cookie check — possession grants access.

  Status pages are now pk-addressed (/StatusAndResults/<pk>/, /StatusUpdate/<pk>/)
  with an ownership check (_load_owned_status_row) that returns an identical
  404 for both "not found" and "not yours" to avoid pk enumeration.

  Housekeeping gains _sweep_orphaned_terminal_rows: TERMINAL rows whose
  file-backed result was trimmed from temp/ are deleted (cascading their
  LRPDispatchData). URL-redirect and empty-redirect rows age out via the
  existing row age-sweep.
